  "solution": {
    "brief": "Surface created from curves",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: Trigonometric surface creation can leverage UV domain remapping for consistent parameterization. The global bounds technique (flatten before Bounds) ensures proper domain scaling across trigonometric functions. UV coordinate systems provide standardized surface parameterization complementing trigonometric approaches.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: High-complexity surface creation: Advanced parametric surface creation workflows can scale up to 73 components (as seen in recipe '14-6'), indicating the potential complexity required for sophisticated trigonometric surface generation.\n\nRelated insight: Recipe 14-8 (34 components) demonstrates that trigonometric surface creation can be achieved with moderate complexity, filling the gap between simple workflows and the high-complexity 73+ component examples.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe complexity mega-complex tier: Unit-01-Class demonstrates that trigonometric parametric surface creation can scale to mega-complex implementations (134 components), far exceeding the previous complexity understanding and suggesting that sophisticated trigonometric surface generation can require extensive computational workflows.",
